 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T21:28+08:00",
 "answer": "**I’d skip a hard or long ride tonight.** The latest Kuching station reading I found was **API 74 (moderate) at 7 pm on Saturday, October 17**, with PM2.5 at 43.6 µg/m³. Another tracker shows a higher reading on a different AQI scale, so conditions may vary by area. ([jerebumalaysia.com](https://jerebumalaysia.com/en/stations/kuching-sarawak/?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you’re generally healthy and still want to cycle, keep it **short and easy**, and turn back if you notice coughing, eye or throat irritation, or shortness of breath. If you have asthma or heart/lung issues—or are especially sensitive to haze—choose indoors instead. Malaysia’s Health Ministry advises people with asthma or haze-related symptoms to avoid going outside until API is below 50. ([moh.gov.my](https://www.moh.gov.my/en/core/health-information/jerebu/artikel-dan-panduan-pengguna-berkaitan-jerebu/kekal-aktif-walaupun-keadaan-berjerebu?utm_source=openai))\n\nThere’s also a chance of **isolated rain tonight**, so check the local forecast before setting out. ([met.gov.my](https://www.met.gov.my/en/forecast/weather/district/Ds504/?utm_source=openai))",
